# Keep line endings sane for anyone who clones this on another platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is normal on Windows and rewrites checked-out text files to
# CRLF. The stored blob is fine, so nothing looks wrong here, but a fresh clone
# on Linux or macOS gets "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" and bash refuses it with
# "bad interpreter: ...^M". Pinning the shell scripts to LF stops that.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf

# The mod reads these at runtime and the game is Windows-only, but a translator
# may edit them on any platform, so keep them LF too.
*.json text eol=lf

*.cs      text
*.csproj  text
*.md      text
*.yml     text

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.ptb binary
*.zip binary
